# Allowlist: ignore everything, then allow only the kinds of files the code is made of.
# Anything else (your settings, data, exports, reports, keys, backups, copies, notes,
# a CLAUDE.md) stays out, whatever it's named. Docs, vendor files and markdown are listed by
# exact name, so a report copied into docs/ can't end up on GitHub Pages. To add a new kind of file, add a "!" line here AND to ALLOWED in
# check_public.py, which enforces the same list on every push.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!*.py
!/README.md
!/coach_prompt.md
!/setup.sh
!*.example.toml
!schema.sql
!LICENSE
!docs/index.html
!docs/privacy.html
!vendor/chart.umd.js
!vendor/chartjs-adapter-date-fns.bundle.min.js

# never, even though they contain .py/.md files
.venv/
__pycache__/
